r industry in the United States and internationally. The company offers outsourced solutions for the development, design, component sourcing and cleaning, prototyping, engineering, and manufacturing and testing of advanced systems. It also provides a range of gas delivery solutions, such as precision thermal products, valves, connectors, industrial process connectors and valves, pneumatic actuators, manifolds and safety solutions, hoses, pressure gauges, gas lines, and component heaters, as well as complex weldments. In addition, the company offers assemblies, including gas and fluid delivery solutions, wafer transport systems, mechatronic assemblies, process modules, and sub-fab process equipment support racks; weldments and frames with exacting standards; heaters, sensors, and controllers for precise temperature control; integrated device manufacturers and OEMs validated process tool chamber parts cleaning and coating services; and tool part process optimization solutions, analytical verification of process tool chamber part cleaning effectiveness and micro contamination analysis of tool parts, wafers and depositions, chemicals, cleanroom materials, deionized water, and airborne molecular contamination. It primarily serves customers in the semiconductor capital equipment and semiconductor integrated device manufacturing industries, as well as display, consumer, medical, energy, industrial, and research equipment industries. The company was founded in 1991 and is headquartered in Hayward, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jinsong  Xiao | CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $990,976 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $296K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $2K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Ultra Clean Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.2B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $15M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 226% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.257877329677297},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $5.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-5338363.07},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): roic below cost of capital; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ultra Clean Holdings (UCTT) Stock Could Be Overvalued After Profit Turn","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ultra-clean-holdings-uctt-stock-121237170.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794485557.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.977,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Did Ultra Clean Holdings (UCTT) Stock Jump After Its Latest Update?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-uctt/ultra-clean-holdings/news/why-did-ultra-clean-holdings-uctt-stock-jump-after-its-lates","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794140669.407,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.932,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Contrasting Ultra Clean (UCTT) and Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/contrasting-ultra-clean-uctt-and-its-competitors.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794136530.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (UCTT) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_UCTT_Volatility_110426010601_1793772361.html","date":